{%- comment -%}
  Article Detail (Figma: Article Detail). Header, hero image, sticky "In this article" list built from the
  article's h2 headings, article body (blockquotes render as the "Doctor’s tip" card), an inline product
  card inserted before a chosen heading, and the medical disclaimer.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign body = article.content
  if body == blank
    assign body = section.settings.fallback_content
  endif
  assign reviewer = article.metafields.lelap.reviewer.value | default: section.settings.reviewer
  assign reviewer_role = article.metafields.lelap.reviewer_role.value | default: section.settings.reviewer_role
  assign read = article.metafields.lelap.read_time.value
  if read == blank
    assign words = body | strip_html | split: ' ' | size
    assign mins = words | divided_by: 200 | at_least: 1
    assign read = 'blogs.article.min_read' | t: count: mins
  endif
  assign topic = article.tags.first
  assign updated = article.updated_at | default: article.published_at

  assign p = section.settings.product
  if p == blank
    assign p = all_products[section.settings.product_handle]
  endif

  capture tip_icon
    render 'icon', name: 'steth', color: '#ffffff', size: 18
  endcapture
  capture tip_open
    echo '<blockquote class="article-tip"><span class="article-tip__icon">'
    echo tip_icon
    echo '</span><div class="article-tip__body"><p class="article-tip__label">'
    echo section.settings.tip_label | escape
    echo '</p>'
  endcapture
  assign body = body | replace: '<blockquote>', tip_open | replace: '</blockquote>', '</div></blockquote>'
  assign parts = body | split: '<h2'
-%}
<article class="article" data-article>
  <header class="article-head">
    <div class="container article-head__inner">
      <p class="article-head__crumbs">
        <a href="{{ blog.url | default: '/blogs/sleep-library' }}">{{ blog.title | default: 'Sleep library' | escape }}</a>
        {%- if topic != blank -%}<span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="{{ blog.url }}/tagged/{{ topic | handleize }}">{{ topic | escape }}</a>{%- endif -%}
      </p>
      <h1 class="article-head__title">{{ article.title | escape }}</h1>
      <div class="article-head__meta">
        {%- if reviewer != blank -%}
          <div class="article-head__reviewer">
            {%- if section.settings.reviewer_image != blank -%}
              {{ section.settings.reviewer_image | image_url: width: 72 | image_tag: width: 36, height: 36, alt: '' }}
            {%- else -%}
              <img src="{{ 'photo-doctor.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="36" height="36">
            {%- endif -%}
            <span><strong>{{ section.settings.reviewed_label | escape }} {{ reviewer | escape }}</strong>{% if reviewer_role != blank %}<small>{{ reviewer_role | escape }}</small>{% endif %}</span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
        <p class="article-head__date">{{ section.settings.updated_label | escape }} {{ updated | date: '%-d %b %Y' }} · {{ read | escape }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="container article-hero">
    {%- if article.image != blank -%}
      {%- assign hero_alt = article.image.alt | default: article.title -%}
      {{ article.image | image_url: width: 2560 | image_tag: loading: 'eager', fetchpriority: 'high', sizes: '(min-width: 1440px) 1280px, 100vw', widths: '600, 900, 1280, 1920, 2560', alt: hero_alt }}
    {%- else -%}
      <img src="{{ section.settings.fallback_image | default: 'photo-phone.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="" width="1280" height="560" fetchpriority="high">
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="container article-body">
    {%- if parts.size > 1 -%}
      <aside class="article-toc" aria-label="{{ section.settings.toc_label | escape }}">
        <p class="article-toc__title">{{ section.settings.toc_label | escape }}</p>
        <ol class="article-toc__list">
          {%- for part in parts offset: 1 -%}
            {%- assign h_html = part | split: '</h2>' | first | prepend: '<h2' | append: '</h2>' -%}
            {%- assign h_text = h_html | strip_html | strip -%}
            <li><a href="#{{ h_text | handleize }}" data-toc-link>{{ h_text }}</a></li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ol>
        <button type="button" class="article-toc__share" data-article-share data-copied="{{ section.settings.copied_label | escape }}">
          {% render 'icon', name: 'share', size: 16 %}<span>{{ section.settings.share_label | escape }}</span>
        </button>
      </aside>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="article-content">
      {%- for part in parts -%}
        {%- if forloop.first -%}
          {{ part }}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign h_html = part | split: '</h2>' | first | prepend: '<h2' | append: '</h2>' -%}
          {%- assign h_text = h_html | strip_html | strip -%}
          {%- assign head_raw = part | split: '</h2>' | first | append: '</h2>' -%}
          {%- if forloop.index0 == section.settings.product_before and section.settings.show_product -%}
            {%- render 'article-product', product: p, product_id: p.id, handle: section.settings.product_handle, text: section.settings.product_text, button: section.settings.product_button, link: section.settings.product_link -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          <h2 id="{{ h_text | handleize }}">{{ h_text }}</h2>
          {{ part | remove_first: head_raw }}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if parts.size <= section.settings.product_before and section.settings.show_product -%}
        {%- render 'article-product', product: p, product_id: p.id, handle: section.settings.product_handle, text: section.settings.product_text, button: section.settings.product_button, link: section.settings.product_link -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.disclaimer != blank -%}
        <p class="article-note">{% render 'icon', name: 'info', size: 16, color: '#5f6179' %}<span>{{ section.settings.disclaimer | escape }}</span></p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
<script src="{{ 'article.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Article",
  "class": "section-main-article",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "reviewed_label", "label": "Reviewed by label", "default": "Medically reviewed by" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "reviewer", "label": "Reviewer", "info": "Article metafield lelap.reviewer overrides this.", "default": "Dr. Ratna Wijaya" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "reviewer_role", "label": "Reviewer role", "info": "Article metafield lelap.reviewer_role overrides this.", "default": "General practitioner" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "reviewer_image", "label": "Reviewer photo" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "updated_label", "label": "Updated label", "default": "Updated" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "fallback_image", "label": "Image when the article has none", "default": "photo-phone.jpg", "options": [
      { "value": "photo-phone.jpg", "label": "Bedside lamp" },
      { "value": "photo-morning.jpg", "label": "Morning stretch" },
      { "value": "photo-ingredients-wide.jpg", "label": "Ingredients" }
    ] },
    { "type": "text", "id": "toc_label", "label": "Contents title", "default": "In this article" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "share_label", "label": "Share label", "default": "Share" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "copied_label", "label": "Link copied label", "default": "Link copied" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tip_label", "label": "Quote label", "info": "Quotes (blockquote) in the article are shown as this tip card.", "default": "Doctor’s tip" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Inline product" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_product", "label": "Show product card", "default": true },
    { "type": "range", "id": "product_before", "label": "Insert before heading number", "min": 1, "max": 12, "step": 1, "default": 5 },
    { "type": "product", "id": "product", "label": "Product" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "product_handle", "label": "Fallback product handle", "default": "sleep-classic" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "product_text", "label": "Product text", "default": "3 mg melatonin, chamomile and L-theanine. Dose set by a doctor." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "product_button", "label": "Button label", "default": "Take the quiz" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "product_link", "label": "Button link", "info": "Defaults to the sleep quiz." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Disclaimer" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "disclaimer", "label": "Disclaimer", "default": "This article is for general information and doesn’t replace advice from your own doctor. Sources reviewed by our medical team are listed below the article." },
    { "type": "html", "id": "fallback_content", "label": "Text shown when the article is empty", "default": "<p>Melatonin isn\u2019t a sleeping pill. It\u2019s a signal. A low dose tells your body clock that night has started, and how well that signal lands depends a lot on what else you do in the evening.</p><h2>Why timing matters</h2><p>Your body starts releasing melatonin about two hours before your usual bedtime. Taking a gummy right as you get into bed means it\u2019s working against the clock instead of with it.</p><blockquote><p>\u201cIf you can only change one thing, change the timing. Most patients who say melatonin doesn\u2019t work are taking it too late.\u201d</p></blockquote><h2>1. Take it 45 minutes early</h2><p>Set a reminder for 45 minutes before you want to be asleep. If your bedtime is 22:30, take it around 21:45.</p><h2>2. Dim the lights at 9pm</h2><p>Bright overhead light, especially cool white LEDs, slows your natural melatonin. Switch to lamps and warm bulbs for the last hour.</p><h2>3. Keep your phone out of bed</h2><p>Charge it across the room. Scrolling keeps your brain alert long after the screen goes dark.</p><h2>4. Eat dinner earlier</h2><p>A heavy meal late at night keeps your body busy digesting. Aim to finish eating at least three hours before bed.</p><h2>5. Keep the room cool</h2><p>Your body temperature drops as you fall asleep. A cool, dark room (around 24\u00b0C with the AC) makes that easier.</p><h2>6. Same bedtime, even on weekends</h2><p>Shifting bedtime by two hours on Saturday is like flying to another time zone. Keep it within an hour if you can.</p><h2>7. Know when to ask for help</h2><p>If you\u2019ve had trouble sleeping for more than three weeks, or you snore loudly and wake up exhausted, talk to a doctor in person. These can be signs of conditions melatonin won\u2019t fix.</p>" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
